// Adversarial: Drift hazard active at 3 stacks with live physics in a Corridor layout,
// stressing the drift_apply_force → apply_bolt_forces pipeline end-to-end.
//
// drift_apply_force runs every FixedUpdate tick and emits ApplyBoltForce messages that
// accelerate the bolt in the configured drift direction. apply_bolt_forces then reads
// those messages and integrates them into Velocity2D. At 3 stacks the force magnitude
// is larger than stack 1, and the force accumulates on every tick — the Corridor layout
// forces hundreds of wall bounces per run, meaning the bolt re-enters the force pipeline
// with a reflected velocity on every bounce. This stresses:
//   - BoltInBounds: if force accumulation is unclamped or the apply step double-integrates,
//     velocity can spike high enough to carry the bolt outside playfield bounds in one tick.
//   - NoNaN: force vector arithmetic on accumulated ApplyBoltForce messages could produce
//     inf or NaN if the message payload is malformed or the reader is double-consumed.
//   - BreakerInBounds: Chaos input at 0.7 drives the breaker to wall edges; combined with
//     high bolt speed from accumulated drift force, the bump geometry exercises the breaker
//     clamping path under asymmetric load.
//   - HazardStackValid: verifies the ActiveHazards entry for Drift retains its stack count
//     across thousands of tick cycles without the entry being zeroed or dropped.
//
// Adversarial conditions:
//   - 3 stacks: exercises per_level scaling beyond stack 1; non-trivial cumulative force
//   - Corridor layout: maximises wall bounces and force-pipeline re-entries per run;
//     the bolt spends more time under continuous drift force than in any other layout
//   - Chaos input (0.7): breaker movement variability forces the force pipeline to
//     accumulate under all bump-quality and bump-angle distributions
//   - disable_physics: false (intentional) — live physics is required to exercise the
//     full drift_apply_force → ApplyBoltForce → apply_bolt_forces → Velocity2D chain;
//     the smoke test (scenarios/mechanic/drift_stack_3_smoke.scenario.ron) uses frozen
//     physics and does not catch force-pipeline bugs
(
    breaker: "Aegis",
    layout: "Corridor",
    input: Chaos((action_prob: 0.7)),
    max_frames: 3000,
    disallowed_failures: [BoltInBounds, BreakerInBounds, HazardStackValid, NoNaN],
    allowed_failures: None,
    debug_setup: None,
    allow_early_end: false,
    seed: 4411,
    frame_mutations: [
        (frame: 30, mutation: InjectHazardStack(kind_name: "Drift", stacks: 3)),
    ],
)
